# Worktree & Deploy Queue Constitution

## Mandatory session worktree (non-negotiable)

**Every delivery session that will write files MUST start in a new isolated worktree.**
Do not implement, test, or build on the MAIN working tree.

| Session type | Placement |
| --- | --- |
| Read-only Q&A (no file writes) | **MAIN** — orchestration only |
| Single mechanical edit (one line/typo; no behavior/API/plan change) | **MAIN** |
| Any behavior-changing or multi-file delivery | **ISOLATED** — **mandatory** |
| `mvn verify` / `pnpm build` / TDD inner loop | **ISOLATED only** — never on MAIN while slices are in flight |
| Doc-sync + commit after slice Done | **MAIN** — only after stage 11 merge |

### Session bootstrap (before first write)

1. **`worktree-router`** — allocate `slice-id`, path, branch; create worktree.
2. **`move_agent_to_root`** — parent and implementers operate in the feature path.
3. Implement → gates → reviews → **`integration-merger`** (stage 11) → merge to `main`.
4. **`post-task-doc-sync`** + **`post-task-commit-review`** on **MAIN** after merge.
5. **`git worktree remove`** + **`prune`** — mandatory cleanup after successful merge.

User same-session opt-out: `main-only`, `no-worktree` (honor immediately; state reason in placement record).

## Naming

| Item | Pattern | Example |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Directory | `../DGE-<slice-id>` | `../DGE-mgmt-ui-defects` |
| Branch | `feat/<slice-id>` | `feat/mgmt-ui-defects` |
| Base | `origin/main` | unless orchestrator names another integration base |

Create (PowerShell, from **MAIN** repo root — MAIN must be clean or stash-first):

```powershell
git fetch origin
git worktree add "..\DGE-<slice-id>" -b feat/<slice-id> origin/main
```

Skill: `.cursor/skills/worktree-isolation/SKILL.md`.

## MAIN worktree role

MAIN is the **integration line**, not the implementation sandbox:

- Orchestration, read-only exploration, merge target.
- Plan/doc-sync/commit **after** `integration-merger`.
- **Forbidden on MAIN during active delivery:** feature code edits, `backend/target` builds, demo docx regeneration, parallel slice WIP.

Shared OK across trees: Git object DB, `~/.m2`, pnpm store.
**Not shared:** working tree, `backend/target/`, `frontend/dist/`, uncommitted files.

## Single Docker host

This machine runs **one** Docker acceptance stack (`8080` / `4173`).

- All deploys use `.\scripts\docker-deploy-queue.ps1` (mutex around `docker-deploy.ps1`).
- Do **not** create a second compose project, port offsets, or parallel stacks.
- If the lock is held: wait or report `DEPLOY_QUEUED` — never bypass.

Skill: `.cursor/skills/docker-deploy-queue/SKILL.md`.

## Pipeline hooks

`delivery-orchestrator` stage **−1** = Batch Recommendation (decide `merge`|`solo`|`split`
into **one** leaf — amortize fixed cost; **not** a second writer). Skill:
`.cursor/skills/delivery-batch-recommend/SKILL.md`.
Stage **0** = provision worktree (always for delivery) for the **single**
`proposed_slice_id`.
Stage **11** = `integration-merger` (merge + remove worktree) **before** doc-sync on MAIN.
See `delivery-orchestration-constitution.mdc`.

Do **not** fold new work into an already sole-active / In Progress leaf — queue the next
leaf serially (Batch Recommendation may still `merge` related *pending* tasks into the
**next** leaf before stage 0).

## Single-lane serial (default, 2026-07-16)

At most **one** delivery leaf may run heavy work (`mvn verify` / full frontend gates /
`docker-deploy-queue` / E2E) at a time. Extra feature worktrees may exist **parked**
(BDD/docs only or idle) but must not run a second writer pipeline unless the user
explicitly says `force-parallel` / `强制并行`.

## Forbidden

- Implementing delivery slices on MAIN (except read-only / single-line exceptions above).
- Two sessions writing the same worktree for different slices.
- Running `mvn verify` or full frontend gates on MAIN while a feature worktree is active.
- Parallel `docker-deploy` from two worktrees.
- Default multitask fan-out of multiple CE leaves (retired; serial queue is default).
- Claiming Done from a feature worktree without merge + MAIN doc-sync.
- Leaving feature worktrees after successful merge without cleanup.
